<td id="S4.T4.2.1.18.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center" style="padding-left:4.0pt;padding-right:4.0pt;">362.46</td>
<td id="S4.T4.2.1.18.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center" style="padding-left:4.0pt;padding-right:4.0pt;">25.23</td>
<td id="S4.T4.2.1.18.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center" style="padding-left:4.0pt;padding-right:4.0pt;">4.17</td></tr>
<tr id="S4.T4.2.1.19" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S4.T4.2.1.19.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left" style="padding-left:4.0pt;padding-right:4.0pt;">Cold-start SFT</td>
<td id="S4.T4.2.1.19.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center" style="padding-left:4.0pt;padding-right:4.0pt;">374.86</td>
<td id="S4.T4.2.1.19.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center" style="padding-left:4.0pt;padding-right:4.0pt;">0.28</td>
<td id="S4.T4.2.1.19.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center" style="padding-left:4.0pt;padding-right:4.0pt;">0.29</td></tr>
<tr id="S4.T4.2.1.20" class="ltx_tr" style="--ltx-bg-color:#E6E6E6;">
<td id="S4.T4.2.1.20.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left" style="padding-left:4.0pt;padding-right:4.0pt;"><span id="S4.T4.2.1.20.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold ltx_font_italic" style="--ltx-bg-color:#E6E6E6;">GSPR</span><span id="S4.T4.2.1.20.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-bg-color:#E6E6E6;"> (safety only)</span></td>
<td id="S4.T4.2.1.20.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center" style="padding-left:4.0pt;padding-right:4.0pt;"><span id="S4.T4.2.1.20.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-bg-color:#E6E6E6;">1374.14</span></td>
<td id="S4.T4.2.1.20.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center" style="padding-left:4.0pt;padding-right:4.0pt;"><span id="S4.T4.2.1.20.3.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-bg-color:#E6E6E6;">31.63</span></td>
<td id="S4.T4.2.1.20.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center" style="padding-left:4.0pt;padding-right:4.0pt;"><span id="S4.T4.2.1.20.4.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-bg-color:#E6E6E6;">3.28</span></td></tr>
<tr id="S4.T4.2.1.21" class="ltx_tr" style="--ltx-bg-color:#E6E6E6;">
<td id="S4.T4.2.1.21.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left" style="padding-left:4.0pt;padding-right:4.0pt;"><span id="S4.T4.2.1.21.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold ltx_font_italic" style="--ltx-bg-color:#E6E6E6;">GSPR</span><span id="S4.T4.2.1.21.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-bg-color:#E6E6E6;"> <span id="S4.T4.2.1.21.1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">w/o</span> Cold-start</span></td>
<td id="S4.T4.2.1.21.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center" style="padding-left:4.0pt;padding-right:4.0pt;"><span id="S4.T4.2.1.21.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-bg-color:#E6E6E6;">172.48</span></td>
<td id="S4.T4.2.1.21.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center" style="padding-left:4.0pt;padding-right:4.0pt;"><span id="S4.T4.2.1.21.3.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-bg-color:#E6E6E6;">15.63</span></td>
<td id="S4.T4.2.1.21.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center" style="padding-left:4.0pt;padding-right:4.0pt;"><span id="S4.T4.2.1.21.4.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-bg-color:#E6E6E6;">0.38</span></td></tr>
<tr id="S4.T4.2.1.22" class="ltx_tr" style="--ltx-bg-color:#E6E6E6;">
<td id="S4.T4.2.1.22.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_bb" style="padding-left:4.0pt;padding-right:4.0pt;"><span id="S4.T4.2.1.22.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold ltx_font_italic" style="--ltx-bg-color:#E6E6E6;">GSPR</span><span id="S4.T4.2.1.22.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-bg-color:#E6E6E6;"> <span id="S4.T4.2.1.22.1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">w/</span> Cold-start</span></td>
<td id="S4.T4.2.1.22.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb" style="padding-left:4.0pt;padding-right:4.0pt;"><span id="S4.T4.2.1.22.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-bg-color:#E6E6E6;">77.73</span></td>
<td id="S4.T4.2.1.22.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb" style="padding-left:4.0pt;padding-right:4.0pt;"><span id="S4.T4.2.1.22.3.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-bg-color:#E6E6E6;">0.04</span></td>
<td id="S4.T4.2.1.22.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb" style="padding-left:4.0pt;padding-right:4.0pt;"><span id="S4.T4.2.1.22.4.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-bg-color:#E6E6E6;">1.00</span></td></tr>
</table>
</span></div>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 4: </span>Statistics of generated responses. Mix % and Repeat % denote the % of responses with language mixing and repetitions, respectively.</figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="S4.SS4.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.SS4.p2.1" class="ltx_p">5) <span id="S4.SS4.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Our GSPR can generate the most efficient safety reasoning traces by introducing its novel category reward and cold-start strategy.</span>
Though ShieldGemma-9B and LlamaGuard3-8B generate the fewest tokens, they cannot provide any justifications for their decisions.
All other models that offer justifications tend to cost more than 140 tokens for safety reasoning.
In contrast, our “<span id="S4.SS4.p2.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">GSPR</span> <span id="S4.SS4.p2.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">w/</span> Cold-start” generates the fewest words with fair explanations for both Qwen2.5 and Qwen3 scenarios.
Furthermore, models that focus solely on safety reward, such as “<span id="S4.SS4.p2.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">GSPR</span> (safety only)” and RSafe, tend to produce more tokens after GRPO alignment.
This difference suggests that our category reward potentially reduces the token cost.
Additionally, even though our cold-start SFT enforces per-policy safety reasoning and naturally leads to more generated tokens.
After subsequent alignment via GRPO, “<span id="S4.SS4.p2.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">GSPR</span> <span id="S4.SS4.p2.1.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">w/o</span> Cold-start” significantly reduces the generation cost to no more than 100 tokens.
Moreover, compare “<span id="S4.SS4.p2.1.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">GSPR</span> <span id="S4.SS4.p2.1.8" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">w/</span> Cold-start” with “<span id="S4.SS4.p2.1.9" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">GSPR</span> <span id="S4.SS4.p2.1.10" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">w/o</span> Cold-start,” the cold-start strategy further reduces the average word by more than half after RL-based alignments.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS4.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.SS4.p3.1" class="ltx_p">6) <span id="S4.SS4.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Our proposed format reward is effective to avoid language switching and verbose repetitions.</span>
Even though RSafe’s generations do not suffer from language mixing and repetitions on the Qwen2.5 base model, with no more than 2% Mix % and Repeat %.
However, when switching to the Qwen3 base model, RSafe and “<span id="S4.SS4.p3.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">GSPR</span> (safety only)” both suffer from more than 25% language mixing ratio and 3% repetition ratio (our “<span id="S4.SS4.p3.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">GSPR</span> (safety only)” follows the exact training procedures as RSafe).
These results imply that RSafe may not be generalizable across models.
In contrast, our <span id="S4.SS4.p3.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">GSPR</span> introduces penalties for language switching and repetitions via reward assignment and results in better generation quality.
However, as shown in “<span id="S4.SS4.p3.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">GSPR</span> <span id="S4.SS4.p3.1.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">w/o</span> Cold-start”, even the explicit penalties are assigned, it is still insufficient to solve Qwen3-8B’s language mixing with 15.63% Mix %.
Fortunately, our cold-start strategy can greatly reduce the language switching to nearly 0% Mix %.
In summary, both the proposed format reward and cold-start strategy are crucial to eliminate language switching and repetitions across various base models.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS4.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.SS4.p4.1" class="ltx_p">For qualitative comparisons, we conduct case studies for both prompt safety moderation and output response moderation. The full results and analyses are shown in Appendix <a href="#A4" title="Appendix D Case Studies ‣ GSPR: Aligning LLM Safeguards as Generalizable Safety Policy Reasoners" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D</span></a>.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S5" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">5 </span>Conclusion</h2>

<div id="S5.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this paper, motivated by training a fine-grained and generalizable safety policy reasoner, we propose <span id="S5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">GSPR</span>, an RL-aligned framework to incentivize LLM guardrails’ fine-grained safety reasoning.
Compared with existing guardrails, our <span id="S5.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">GSPR</span> incorporates a flexible training prompt with safety policy variables.
During training, our <span id="S5.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">GSPR</span> proposes a tailored cold-start SFT strategy and implements careful format controls with category rewards for guardrails’ rollouts.
Our experimental results indicate that our <span id="S5.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">GSPR</span> achieves state-of-the-art safety prediction and category prediction performance.
Moreover, our analysis suggests that our <span id="S5.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">GSPR</span> has the least token cost for safety reasoning with the least corrupted responses.
For future work, we plan to integrate more existing safety benchmarks as our training data to further improve the safety generalization ability of <span id="S5.p1.1.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">GSPR</span>.</p>
</div>
<div class="ltx_pagination ltx_role_newpage"></div>
</section>
